# Smoke tests

`t/smoke.t` exercises the plugin's REST API endpoints and `opac_js` output. It
is GET-only and does not modify plugin configuration or patron/item data; it
skips cleanly if the plugin is not installed.

## Requirements

- The plugin is installed and enabled in the target Koha instance.
- `KOHA_CONF` points to the instance's `koha-conf.xml`.

## Run

    KOHA_CONF=/etc/koha/sites/<instance>/koha-conf.xml \
    PERL5LIB=/usr/share/koha/lib \
    prove -I/var/lib/koha/<instance>/plugins t/smoke.t

Or run the test directly:

    KOHA_CONF=/etc/koha/sites/<instance>/koha-conf.xml \
    PERL5LIB=/usr/share/koha/lib \
    perl -I/var/lib/koha/<instance>/plugins t/smoke.t
